  "special_value_policy": "Finite vectors require exact FP32 bits. Explicit nonfinite vectors compare classification only, not NaN payload. Normal comparator requires finite values.",
  "zero_policy": "Native MXFP4 GGML/Maya integer E2M1 tables map nibble0/8 to +0; ideal signed E2M1 is not this native scalar contract. F32 and MXFP8 signed zero are preserved. Raw bytes are never rewritten.",
  "MXFP8_scale_policy": "Fixed Maya FP32 scale = castFP32(2^(e-127)) before FP32 code*scale. e255 scale overflows +inf; zero code gives NaN and half/nonzero code gives inf. This candidate contract is distinct from ideal OCP/reserved exponent semantics and other possible converters."
